},{"date":"2014-11-17T08:52:01-08:00","id":314553,"title":"","content":"I consider myself a Moderate Right Wing as well. <br /> <br /> Nevertheless, the definition between Right/Left seems to be quite different in the USA than in Europe. And in the Thread of the Left there was a test that, by the questions asked, portrayed every Wright Winger as a Inhuman Sadistic Bastard.<br /> <br /> In my view and the main reason I tend on the Right is simply because without Right you have no Left. The ideals of the Left are beautiful indeed, but people forget that you need a strong economy and generate money in order to pursue them.<br /> <br /> A degree of authoritarianism and strong economical policies are necessary, but that shouldn't take the focus that it is only beneficial while it is applied to the betterment of the citizens Governments <b>serve</b>. Above all liberty must always be respected. <br /> <br /> And it is explained by History, especially in my country, every time there is trouble and state lacks money, it's a Right Wing party that takes power until things are good again. Then the people call them assholes for all the harsh measures, vote for a Left Wing to distribute privileges until the State needs money again and a Right Wing Party... well you get the point.<br /> <br /> It is very hard to explain one's views in so few words and I hope everyone reads this with a grain of salt. Despite my views one thing I will ALWAYS oppose: Extremists. Doesn't matter if it's Libertarianism/Authoritarianism/Left/Right, it's always wrong. Bringing it to the middle as best as possible is what makes it work for the best. I don't want a libertarian running my country nor do I want a dictator, I believe in capitalism but with rules and state intervention. It's all about reaching an equilibrium and what you need at different times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T09:05:03-08:00","id":314585,"title":"","content":"Left-wing-Right-wing tends to change over time in the US.<br /> <br /> &quot;Left&quot; (progressive) was typically democrat, while &quot;right&quot; (conservative) was republican.<br /> <br /> As an example, Eisenhower (mid 1950s Republican) had this as a platform;<br /> <i><br /> 1. Provide federal assistance to low-income communities;<br /> <br /> 2. Protect Social Security;<br /> <br /> 3. Provide asylum for refugees;<br /> <br /> 4. Extend minimum wage;<br /> <br /> 5. Improve unemployment benefit system so it covers more people;<br /> <br /> 6. Strengthen labor laws so workers can more easily join a union;<br /> <br /> 7. Assure equal pay for equal work regardless of sex.</i><br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> That platform is very different today, and is supposed to fall under the Democrats, but today...everything has shifted right-ward, so we're looking at a lot of caveats.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T09:16:05-08:00","id":314617,"title":"","content":"In my country that platform falls under EVERY party's policy, from left to right, those objects are in everyone's political speech. Well except for 6th, but our labour laws have always been so strict and over protectionist they are now being loosened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T10:01:57-08:00","id":314661,"title":"","content":"Why not just make a Politics thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T10:07:04-08:00","id":314666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/314378-the-right-wing-thread?p=314661#post314661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just make a Politics thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that's a silly question.","