\">And in the Thread of the Left there was a test that, by the questions asked, portrayed every Wright Winger as a Inhuman Sadistic Bastard.</div> </div> </div> </div>The people who usually create and spread tests like that one are Right-leaning Libertarians looking for common ground with Individualists from both Right and Left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T13:03:36-08:00","id":314780,"title":"","content":"And answering why I consider myself right wing, in my own perception:<br /> <br /> - liberal views on economy, but tempered with common sense<br /> - my reluctance against expanding social spending. I'm more for rationally managing expenditure rather than throw more money as a solution. In long term social expenditure should be decreased if money is spend effectively on giving the rod rather than the fish, as less people would need social aid. No elimination of social aid, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom