class=\"message\">And answering why I consider myself right wing, in my own perception:<br /> <br /> - liberal views on economy, but tempered with common sense<br /> - my reluctance against expanding social spending. I'm more for rationally managing expenditure rather than throw more money as a solution. In long term social expenditure should be decreased if money is spend effectively on giving the rod rather than the fish, as less people would need social aid. No elimination of social aid, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> THIS! This needs to be explained to every dumbass politician out there! Starting with the ones in this corner of EU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}